# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. Phase 1 through Phase 11 are complete. See [docs/phase-11.md](docs/phase-11.md). Locked sequence after that is [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md). Next build item is Fly.io (roadmap 1). Do not write `phase-fly.md` or start Fly.io until Click asks.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 11 is the first managing playbook. Type `dca` on the desk. Same `futures_*` ledger and `runFuturesCommand`. The app owns orders and exits. Signals only arm. Stacked playbooks, one per contract and side. Do not add a Fly.io worker until roadmap 1 starts. Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the in-app ledger.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture. Do not start Fly.io, Hyperliquid, copy trading, scale-in, MEXC, or onboarding wizard refine until Click starts that roadmap item. Hyperliquid is roadmap 2 ([docs/phase-hyperliquid.md](docs/phase-hyperliquid.md)). Scale-in / position builder is roadmap 6, not “Phase 12”. See [docs/phase-onboarding.md](docs/phase-onboarding.md) (roadmap 9).

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
